From a91ed5a0c4d5b99db20164fcfc72a7e5f9155249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:55:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/libopenh264enc: map constrained baseline to
 PRO_BASELINE

AV_PROFILE_H264_CONSTRAINED_BASELINE includes FFmpeg's constraint flag
and has the value 578. OpenH264 expects an EProfileIdc enumerator, not
the FFmpeg profile value with constraint flags. Passing 578 causes an
invalid enum load in OpenH264 parameter validation.

Translate constrained baseline to PRO_BASELINE at the API boundary.
Keep the FFmpeg profile and the existing CAVLC selection unchanged.
Main and high profile values are unaffected.

Reproduced with UBSan in the existing OpenH264 encoder tests.
---
 libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c b/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
index 6f6f264636..37621cb207 100644
--- a/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
@@ -220,7 +220,8 @@ static av_cold int svc_encode_init(AVCodecContext *avctx)
     param.sSpatialLayers[0].fFrameRate          = param.fMaxFrameRate;
     param.sSpatialLayers[0].iSpatialBitrate     = param.iTargetBitrate;
     param.sSpatialLayers[0].iMaxSpatialBitrate  = param.iMaxBitrate;
-    param.sSpatialLayers[0].uiProfileIdc        = s->profile;
+    param.sSpatialLayers[0].uiProfileIdc        = s->profile == AV_PROFILE_H264_CONSTRAINED_BASELINE ?
+                                                PRO_BASELINE : s->profile;
 
 #if OPENH264_VER_AT_LEAST(1, 7)
     if (avctx->sample_aspect_ratio.num && avctx->sample_aspect_ratio.den) {
-- 
